DOS-PORT (patch 0097, Phase 9 wave 23 W23A). Implements Path B —
tilemap caching for the wave-22 W22A2-measured mds_tilemap_fg
(14-17 ms in gameplay) and mds_tilemap_bg (3-13 ms across scenes)
brackets which together account for 83-88% of mode_draw_scene per
docs/PHASE11-WAVE-22-FINDINGS.md § 11.4. Plus bundles sdl-engine's
keyboard-fix diagnostic (5 mandatory fields appended to existing
kbd/audio block log line) per team-lead's scope-addendum decision —
combined iter answers two questions in one cycle.

Authored against:
  - docs/PHASE11-WAVE-23-DESIGN.md § 1-12 (cache architecture)
  - docs/PHASE11-WAVE-23-CONTRACT.md § 1-9 (cache instrumentation)
  - docs/PHASE11-KEYBOARD-DIAGNOSTIC-SPEC.md § 1-9 (kbd diagnostic)
All three docs gitignored (workspace-local).

Path B is the wave-23 ranked-1 candidate per
docs/PHASE11-WAVE-22-FINDINGS.md § 11.6 — refuted Path A (drawcall
batching, mds_object_loop = 0.4-0.8 ms cap) and Path C (dirty-rect
within DrawScene, regression-class per
memory/wave_17_4_partial_flush_regression.md). Real-HW probe data
(memcpy76k = 17.0 MB/s = 4.3 ms cache-blit cost; colorkey'd FG ~7.7
ms ceiling) anchors the gain projection: ~10 ms savings per cache hit
on Mimiga FG, ~10 ms on attract BG. Adaptive-α (Option α) auto-
disables a layer's cache when miss-render-cost < 2 × hit-cost
(8.6 ms BG / 15.4 ms FG thresholds) for 10 consecutive frames —
prevents per-scene regressions on attract FG (1.21 ms) + First Cave
BG (3.56 ms) where caching would regress baseline.

Implementation:

1. **NEW Renderer::drawCachedTilemap(SDL_Surface *src, bool with_-
   colorkey)** in graphics/Renderer.{h,cpp}. Sibling to patch 0080's
   drawCachedBackdrop. Single SDL_BlitSurface from cache surface to
   window surface, plus 1 _record_dirty_rect call. Replaces the per-
   tile drawTile loop in map_draw() on cache hit. Color-key state
   lives on src->flags — caller (map.cpp) sets it on FG cache surface
   only; SDL_BlitSurface auto-dispatches.

2. **NEW Tileset::drawTileToSurface(SDL_Surface *dst, int dst_x,
   int dst_y, int t)** in graphics/Tileset.{h,cpp}. Raw blit from
   tileset to arbitrary destination surface, bypassing Renderer
   overhead. Used during cache miss-render to populate cache. Mirrors
   patch 0080's pattern (raw SDL_BlitSurface at cache fill time, no
   _DrawcallTimer / no _record_dirty_rect / no per-call _bump_drawcall).

3. **Cache architecture** in map.cpp:
   - 2 SDL_Surface* (BG opaque INDEX8, FG colorkey'd INDEX8)
   - Cache key tuple per layer: (curmap, scroll_x, scroll_y,
     flipacceltime!=0, tile_mutation_counter, w, h, format)
   - Lazy-alloc on first miss; released on map_flush_graphics() via
     NXE::Diag::tilemap_cache_reset() hook
   - 3 helper functions: _tilemap_render_plain_tiles_into_cache (miss
     path; raw blits via Tileset::drawTileToSurface),
     _tilemap_render_special_tiles_to_window (live overlay for
     TA_CURRENT + 0x43 cells; runs on every frame regardless of
     cache hit/miss),
     _tilemap_render_uncached_full_loop (killswitch / disabled-by-
     adaptive-α path; original per-tile loop preserved verbatim)
   - Three render paths: uncached / cache-hit / cache-miss (per
     contract § 3.2 spec for killswitch-disabled state shows
     bg_h=0 bg_m=0 — counter increments NOT made on uncached path)

4. **Architectural deviation from design § 4** (transparently flagged
   to team-lead in pre-format-patch DM, explicit team-lead approval
   landed before format-patch):
   - Design § 4 specified `motionpos*has_current` in cache key with
     `has_visible_current_tiles` detection flag.
   - **Implementation: TA_CURRENT animated water-current cells AND
     0x43 destructible cells render LIVE every frame (via
     `_tilemap_render_special_tiles_to_window`) and are NOT cached.
     motionpos is NOT in cache key.**
   - Why: bypass-not-key keeps cache hit rate HIGH on motion-tile
     maps (Almond, Reservoir) — cache stays valid even when motionpos
     changes every tick. With motionpos in key, those maps would see
     ~0% hit rate. Live-overlay cost is small (sparse animated tiles
     ~5-10 visible per map; ~0.1-0.5 ms overhead per frame) vs full-
     miss-render (14-17 ms). Avoids `has_visible_current_tiles`
     detection complexity. Per `pressure_test_tidy_narratives.md`
     handles the quiescent-edge case (motion-tile maps) better than
     original design. team-lead approval recorded: "TA_CURRENT
     animated tiles + 0x43 destructible cells render LIVE every
     frame, NOT cached. motionpos NOT in cache key. Approved."
   - Risks for findings analysis: if motion-tile maps have more
     animated tiles than expected, live overlay cost could grow
     beyond 0.5 ms; render order must draw live-overlay on top of
     cached plain-tile pass for visual correctness. Both testable in
     W23A iter.

5. **Adaptive-α state machine** (per design § 5 Option α):
   - Per-layer `g_tilemap_*_consecutive_low_misses` counter (file-
     scope in map.cpp anonymous namespace).
   - On miss with `dt < threshold_ns`: increment; if counter reaches
     10, transition `*_enabled` to false + bump
     `disable_transitions_block` + LOG_INFO + reset counter.
   - On miss with `dt >= threshold` OR on hit: reset counter to 0.
   - Re-armed via `tilemap_cache_reset()` on map_flush_graphics().
   - Thresholds: TILEMAP_BG_MISS_THRESHOLD_NS = 8,600,000 (8.6 ms =
     2× memcpy76k 4.3 ms); TILEMAP_FG_MISS_THRESHOLD_NS = 15,400,000
     (15.4 ms = 2× colorkey'd-blit 7.7 ms ceiling). Hardcoded per
     probe data § 11.6.

6. **Tile mutation counter** — `g_tile_mutation_counter` (file-scope
   in map.cpp anonymous namespace) bumped by `map_ChangeTileWithSmoke`
   at the existing `map.tiles[x][y] = newtile;` mutation site.

7. **Killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILEMAP_CACHE=0** (strict-0,
   default ON) per contract § 3.2:
   - NEW `_strict_falsy_env()` helper in Renderer.cpp anonymous
     namespace (sibling to `_strict_truthy_env`); returns true ONLY
     on env value "0".
   - NEW `_abl_tilemap_cache_killswitch()` env helper wraps
     `_strict_falsy_env("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_TILEMAP_CACHE")` with
     cached static-const-bool — -O2 hoists per-frame guards.
   - NEW NXE::Diag::tilemap_cache_killswitch_active() forward-decl
     accessor (file-top wrapper) + definition at file-scope-after-
     both-namespace-closes block (mirrors W20B/W22A/W22.5 trap-and-
     fix pattern). map.cpp short-circuits via this accessor.

8. **13-field hit/miss counter line** per contract § 1.2 + § 2.2:
   - `[mds-tilemap-cache n=N bg_h=H bg_m=M bg_state=E|D bg_t=T
     fg_h=H fg_m=M fg_state=E|D fg_t=T bg_ms_h=N.NN bg_ms_m=N.NN
     fg_ms_h=N.NN fg_ms_m=N.NN]`
   - 13 storage variables in NXE::Diag (extern in
     diagnostic_timers.h, defined in Renderer.cpp).
   - Per-block reset of 12 counters AFTER emit; 2 sticky `*_enabled`
     flags NOT reset per block (only flipped by adaptive-α state
     machine or `tilemap_cache_reset()` on map change).
   - Mean ms = total_ns / 1e6 / count; computed inline in format
     string. No p50/p95 per flush-instr's contract decision —
     running-sum + count sufficient for v1 cache-effectiveness
     analysis.
   - Counter emission gates on EXISTING SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MODE_DRAW_-
     SCENE_INSTR=1 (W22.5 hint) per contract § 3.1; killswitch only
     affects cache architecture, NOT counter emit.
   - `n` counter increments at start of DrawScene() in game.cpp
     (NOT per Game::tick) per contract § 5.

9. **bg_state/fg_state field renders factor BOTH killswitch AND
   adaptive-α sticky enabled flag** (post-build-qa-smoke-C fix —
   see § 9.b below):
   - `_bg_state_char = (killswitch_active || !g_tilemap_bg_cache_-
     enabled) ? 'D' : 'E'`; same for fg.
   - Killswitch wins at render time WITHOUT mutating the sticky
     `*_enabled` flag (which preserves adaptive-α semantics).
   - Per contract § 3.2: "killswitch-disabled: BOTH bg_state=D AND
     fg_state=D from BLOCK 1 (no transition history)" — required
     for flush-instr's analysis tooling to distinguish killswitch-
     disabled (state=D from block 1) from adaptive-α-disabled
     (starts state=E, transitions via state=D).

   9.a. Pre-fix behavior (drafted): state field rendered ONLY the
        sticky enabled flag. Under killswitch (which short-circuits
        cache lookup in map.cpp), the sticky flag stayed true, so
        smoke C showed bg_state=E in 61/61 blocks despite cache
        being bypassed.
   9.b. build-qa W23A smoke C surfaced this deviation per silent-
        narrow rule (their STOP-and-ack to nx-engine before claiming
        Task #23 complete). Fix: render-time only — does NOT mutate
        `g_tilemap_*_cache_enabled` (preserves adaptive-α semantics
        for the layered-disable path). Counter behavior (canonical
        killswitch-engaged indicator) was already correct pre-fix;
        this fix only restores contract-literal compliance for the
        state field.

10. **Keyboard-fix diagnostic** per
    docs/PHASE11-KEYBOARD-DIAGNOSTIC-SPEC.md § 1-9:
    - 5 mandatory fields (pic1_mask_live, kbd_8042_stat,
      bios_kbd_head, bios_kbd_tail, bios_kbd_buf0) appended to
      existing kbd/audio block log line at Renderer.cpp:1128.
    - Inlined `DOS_PeekUint16` body via raw `_farpeekw(_dos_ds, ...)`
      per sdl-engine spec § 8 open invitation — avoids cross-vendor
      relative include of vendor/SDL/src/core/dos/SDL_dos.h.
    - Optional field 6 (`idt_int9_pm_off`) SKIPPED — Renderer.cpp
      doesn't currently include `<dpmi.h>` / `<go32.h>`. The 5
      mandatory fields disambiguate spec § 5 triage table.
    - Default-emit per spec § 7.3 — no env-var gate.
    - Existing 8 fields preserved verbatim (no rename/reorder).
    - sdl-engine review of placement: APPROVED end-to-end.

Build-fix flag: initial build linker-error'd on `(anonymous
namespace)::flipacceltime` — putting `extern int flipacceltime;`
inside the anonymous namespace silently bound it to anonymous-
namespace linkage. Fixed by declaring `extern int flipacceltime;`
at GLOBAL scope above the anonymous namespace, referenced via
`::flipacceltime` qualification.

Memory overhead: ~154 KB heap (76,800 × 2 cache surfaces + ~80
bytes static state). Trivial on g2k Tier-1 (0.3% of 48 MB).

